course: dictionary
lesson: 11395
title: Accessible: easy to reach, use or understand
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Accessible has three main meanings. It can mean easy to reach or get into, easy to use for people who have disabilities, or easy to understand. Read the words around it to find which one fits. «The island is accessible only by boat» means you can only get there by boat.
explain: Clues help you choose. «The new library is wheelchair accessible, with a ramp at the front and a lift to every floor.» The ramp and lift are the clues: people who use wheelchairs can get in and move around. Ask yourself: what would make this easy for people to reach or use?
explain: Accessible can also describe words. «Mr Patel wrote an accessible science book, with short sentences and clear pictures.» Here the clues are short sentences and clear pictures, so accessible means easy to understand. Try swapping in "easy to understand". If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Look for phrases too: accessible to everyone, easily accessible and accessible by car. Words that go together often help you. If you are not sure, check a dictionary.
fact: Accessible means easy to reach, enter or use.
fact: Accessible can also mean easy to use for people with disabilities, for example with ramps, lifts or large print.
fact: Accessible can mean easy to understand, as in «an accessible explanation».
fact: «Wheelchair accessible» means a place that people in wheelchairs can get into and use.
fact: Good phrases to remember: accessible to everyone, easily accessible, accessible by car.
exercise: «The island is accessible only by boat.» What does accessible mean here? | *Easy to reach | Very big and flat | Hidden under the sea | Covered in snow
exercise: «The new hall is wheelchair accessible, with a ramp and a lift.» What does accessible mean? | Free to rent for parties | Very noisy at night | *Easy to get into and use for people with disabilities | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «The teacher gave an accessible explanation, with pictures and simple words.» What does accessible mean here? | Very long and boring | Given only to older children | *Easy to understand | Written in a foreign language
test: «Is the park accessible by bus?» What is the question asking? | *Can people get to the park easily by bus? | Is the park painted blue? | Does the park have a shop? | Is the park very old?
test: «The new book is accessible, with large print and short words.» What does accessible mean here? | Written in code that no one knows | *Easy to read and understand | Very expensive to buy | Only sold near the sea
exam: What is the best meaning of accessible in «The museum is accessible to everyone»? | Closed on Sundays | Full of very old things | Only open to adults | *Easy for everyone to reach and use
